# Azure Site-to-Site VPN with Terraform

This repository contains a Terraform configuration for building a Site-to-Site VPN lab on Microsoft Azure.

The project is based on a networking lab and was created as part of my cloud and infrastructure training.

## Architecture

The lab connects an on-premises network to an Azure virtual network through an IPsec/IKEv2 Site-to-Site VPN.

```text
On-Premises
10.10.10.0/24
      |
   ROUTER01
      |
   IPsec / IKEv2
      |
Azure VPN Gateway
      |
10.20.20.0/24
      |
   Server-B
10.20.20.20
```

## Main Components

- Azure Virtual Network
- Azure VPN Gateway
- Azure Local Network Gateway
- IPsec Site-to-Site VPN connection
- Azure Network Interface
- Debian Linux virtual machine
- Terraform
- AzureRM Provider

## Technologies

- Terraform
- Microsoft Azure
- AzureRM Provider
- IPsec / IKEv2
- strongSwan
- Debian Linux
- nginx

## Project Structure

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| `network.tf` | Azure virtual network and subnets |
| `public_ip.tf` | Public IP address for the VPN Gateway |
| `vpn_gateway.tf` | Azure VPN Gateway |
| `local_network_gateway.tf` | On-premises network definition |
| `vpn_connection.tf` | Site-to-Site VPN connection |
| `server_b_nic.tf` | Network interface for Server-B |
| `server_b_vm.tf` | Server-B virtual machine |
| `variables.tf` | Terraform variables |
| `locals.tf` | Common local values |
| `provider.tf` | Azure provider configuration |
| `versions.tf` | Terraform and provider version constraints |
| `data.tf` | Azure resource group data source |

## Security

Sensitive values such as the VPN pre-shared key are provided through environment variables and are not committed to the repository.

Example:

```bash
export TF_VAR_vpn_shared_key='CHANGE_ME'
```

The `.env` file is excluded from Git.

## Usage

Initialize Terraform:

```bash
terraform init
```

Check the configuration:

```bash
terraform validate
```

Review the execution plan:

```bash
terraform plan
```

Apply the configuration:

```bash
terraform apply
```

## Purpose

The main purpose of this project is to practice:

- Infrastructure as Code with Terraform
- Azure networking
- Site-to-Site VPN configuration
- IPsec/IKEv2 concepts
- Linux network routing
- Cloud infrastructure troubleshooting

This repository is primarily a learning and lab project.
